CAT = "ukaplhDps"; SEG = "DPS"
Q = [
("What is the main role of the designated premises supervisor?",
 "Day-to-day control of the premises", ["Holding the lease on the building", "Checking IDs at the main door", "Inspecting other licensed venues"],
 "The DPS is the person named on the premises licence who has day-to-day responsibility for the premises and is the main contact for the police and licensing authority."),
("What must a designated premises supervisor hold?",
 "A personal licence", ["A premises licence", "An SIA door licence", "A club certificate"],
 "The DPS must hold a valid personal licence. If their personal licence is suspended or revoked, no alcohol can be sold under the premises licence until a new DPS is in place."),
("How many designated premises supervisors can a premises licence name?",
 "One", ["Two", "Three", "One per bar"],
 "A premises licence names only one DPS, however large the premises or however many bars it has."),
("Can one person be the DPS for more than one premises?",
 "Yes, the law sets no limit", ["No, only one premises", "Only two premises at once", "Only within one council area"],
 "The Act does not limit how many premises one person can supervise, but the licensing authority and police will want to see that they can genuinely exercise control at each."),
("Must the DPS be on the premises whenever it is open?",
 "No, it is not required", ["Yes, whenever it is open", "Yes, whenever alcohol is sold", "Only on Friday and Saturday"],
 "The law does not require the DPS to be present at all times. Statutory guidance expects them to be contactable and to have authorised the staff who sell alcohol."),
("The premises has no DPS, or the DPS's personal licence is suspended. What follows?",
 "No alcohol may be sold", ["Sales continue for 28 days", "Sales continue until 11 pm", "Any manager may authorise"],
 "A mandatory condition says no alcohol may be supplied while there is no DPS or while the DPS does not hold a valid personal licence."),
("Who applies to the licensing authority to change the DPS?",
 "The premises licence holder", ["The new DPS on their own", "The outgoing DPS in writing", "The local police licensing unit"],
 "The premises licence holder applies to vary the licence to name a new DPS, with the new DPS's signed consent. The outgoing DPS has no part in the application."),
("Who must give written consent before being named as the DPS?",
 "The proposed DPS", ["The local police", "The licensing committee", "The previous DPS"],
 "The proposed DPS must sign a consent form agreeing to take on the role. It goes with the application to the licensing authority."),
("How long do the police have to object to a change of DPS?",
 "14 days", ["3 days", "7 days", "28 days"],
 "The police have 14 days from being notified to object, and only in exceptional circumstances where the change would undermine the crime prevention objective."),
("When can a new DPS start before the change application is decided?",
 "When immediate effect is requested", ["Only after a council hearing is held", "Only after the 28-day notice ends", "Only once the police have agreed"],
 "The premises licence holder can ask for the change to take immediate effect when the application is received. If the police later object and the authority refuses, the change is reversed."),
("A DPS wants to stop being the DPS for a pub. What must they do?",
 "Notify the licensing authority", ["Simply stop working there", "Ask the police to remove them", "Hand back their personal licence"],
 "A DPS can remove themselves by giving notice to the licensing authority. Their personal licence is unaffected."),
("A DPS gives notice to remove themselves. Within how long must they give the premises licence holder a copy?",
 "48 hours", ["24 hours", "7 days", "14 days"],
 "The DPS must give the premises licence holder a copy of the notice within 48 hours, so the holder knows to stop alcohol sales until a new DPS is named."),
("Which premises can apply to have no DPS?",
 "A community village hall", ["A nightclub with late hours", "A supermarket off-licence", "A hotel residents' bar"],
 "Community premises such as church and village halls run by a committee can apply to remove the DPS requirement, so the management committee is responsible for alcohol sales instead."),
("Why does statutory guidance say premises selling alcohol must have a DPS?",
 "So authorities have a clear contact", ["So staff can legally be trained", "So the premises can open late", "So the licence fee is lower"],
 "The guidance explains the DPS ensures there is always one specified individual who can be contacted quickly by the police, the authority or fire services if problems arise."),
("Where is the designated premises supervisor named?",
 "On the premises licence", ["On the personal licence", "On the fire risk assessment", "On the staff noticeboard"],
 "The DPS's name appears on the premises licence and its summary. Their own personal licence does not name any premises."),
("Can the premises licence holder also be the DPS?",
 "Yes, with a personal licence", ["No, never the same person", "Only with police approval", "Only at a members' club"],
 "An individual who holds the premises licence can also be the DPS if they hold a personal licence. Clubs operating under a club premises certificate do not have a DPS at all."),
]
